sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Client as Postman
  participant GW as Traefik Gateway
  participant HR as HTTPRoute control-api
  participant SVC as Service control-api<br/>(active) / -preview (green)
  participant API as control-api pod
  participant PG as PostgreSQL<br/>control + workflow schemas
  participant DBZ as Debezium
  participant K as Kafka<br/>provisioning.commands.v1
  participant ORCH as orchestrator
  participant PROV as proxmox-provider

  Client->>GW: POST /v1/projects/{id}/instances<br/>Host: control-plane.test<br/>Idempotency-Key
  GW->>HR: match rules
  alt Header X-Canary: green
    HR->>SVC: control-api-preview
  else No canary header
    HR->>SVC: control-api
  end
  SVC->>API: forward

  API->>API: verify JWT, role, project membership
  API->>PG: BEGIN
  API->>PG: advisory lock on the idempotency scope
  alt Key already used with the same payload
    PG-->>API: stored response
    API-->>Client: 202 replayed = true
  else First use of this key
    API->>PG: instance, operation, IPv4 lease,<br/>audit entry, outbox row
    API->>PG: COMMIT
    API-->>Client: 202 { operationId, targetId, statusUrl }
  end

  Note over PG,K: The command is committed before it is published.<br/>Nothing is sent that the database did not accept.

  PG->>DBZ: logical replication of control.outbox
  DBZ->>K: instance.create.requested
  K->>ORCH: consume
  ORCH->>PG: admit command, claim under lease + fencing token
  ORCH->>PROV: gRPC provider calls, one stage per claim
  PROV-->>ORCH: task results
  ORCH->>PG: checkpoint each stage, then complete
  PG->>DBZ: workflow.outbox
  DBZ->>K: instance.mutation.completed
  K->>API: projection consumer applies the read model

  Client->>GW: GET .../operations/{operationId}
  GW-->>Client: 200 { state: succeeded }
